<title>BELGIUM: BBL raises Cockerill to speculative buy.</title>
<headline>BBL raises Cockerill to speculative buy.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of research report -</p>
<p>Co name-----------Sector------Price------Broker-------------</p>
<p>    Cockerill Sambre  Steel	 124 *  BBL/Vermeulen-Raemdonck</p>
<p>COMMENT: Cockerill Sambre well positioned to benefit from any upturn in European steel prices, with focus on high value- added products. Net gearing at end of 1996 around 27 percent, one of lowest in industry. Cumulative preferred dividends offer potential high yield. Free cash flow valuation of share gives range 142/160 francs. BBL short-term target price: 150 francs.</p>
<p>Recommendation: SPECULATIVE BUY Analyst: Olivier Heuschling</p>
<p>(*) Date of research report: 26/02/97</p>
<p> Estimates:   EPS	  pvs est   P/E   Gross dividend</p>
<p> 1995	   17.7 BFR   n/a	 10.1    25.3 BFR</p>
<p> 1996	   -7.0 BFR   n/a	  n/a     0   BFR</p>
<p> 1997	    3.1 BFR   n/a	 37.2    18.0 BFR</p>
<p> 1998	   11.9 BFR   n/a	 10.5    18.0 BFR</p>
